<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 4.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 4.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 10/04/96  09/27/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    205.15    198.70    88.22	85.44     93.30</p>
<p>West	    232.95    230.42    88.33	87.37     92.10</p>
<p>Total Canada  438.10    429.11    88.27	86.46     92.20</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 10/04/96: 232.31 bcf, 09/27/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 10/04/96: 263.74 bcf, 09/27/96: 263.74 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
